<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Deciles and percentiles of grouped data</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>The table shows the marks of \({@n@}\) learners in a county mock examination.</p><table border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><tr><th style="padding:4px 10px;">Mark</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">{@lo[1]@}–{@hi[1]@}</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">{@lo[2]@}–{@hi[2]@}</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">{@lo[3]@}–{@hi[3]@}</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">{@lo[4]@}–{@hi[4]@}</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">{@lo[5]@}–{@hi[5]@}</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">{@lo[6]@}–{@hi[6]@}</th></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">Frequency (\(f\))</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[1]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[2]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[3]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[4]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[5]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[6]@}</td></tr></table><p>(a) Find the decile \(D_{ {@k@} }\), correct to 1 decimal place.</p><div>\(D_{ {@k@} } =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) Find the percentile \(P_{ {@j@} }\), correct to 1 decimal place.</p><div>\(P_{ {@j@} } =\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>For grouped data the decile \(D_k\) is at position \(kn/10\) and the percentile \(P_j\) at \(jn/100\). Then use the same formula as for quartiles, \(L + \dfrac{\text{position} - CF}{F} \times c\), with \(L\) the lower class boundary (the marks are whole numbers, so the class {@lo[1]@}–{@hi[1]@} starts at \({@exd(lcb[1])@}\)).</p><table border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><tr><th style="padding:4px 10px;">Class</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">Frequency (\(f\))</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">Cumulative frequency (cf)</th></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@lo[1]@}–{@hi[1]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[1]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@cf[1]@}</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@lo[2]@}–{@hi[2]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[2]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@cf[2]@}</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@lo[3]@}–{@hi[3]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[3]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@cf[3]@}</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@lo[4]@}–{@hi[4]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[4]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@cf[4]@}</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@lo[5]@}–{@hi[5]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[5]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@cf[5]@}</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@lo[6]@}–{@hi[6]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[6]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@cf[6]@}</td></tr></table><p>(a) \(D_{ {@k@} }\) is at position \({@k@} \times {@n@} \div 10 = {@exd(pd)@}\), in the class {@lo[kD]@}–{@hi[kD]@}: \[D_{ {@k@} } = {@exd(lcb[kD])@} + \frac{ {@exd(pd)@} - {@cfb(kD)@} }{ {@f[kD]@} } \times 10 \approx {@Dd@}\]</p><p>(b) \(P_{ {@j@} }\) is at position \({@j@} \times {@n@} \div 100 = {@exd(pp)@}\), in the class {@lo[kP]@}–{@hi[kP]@}: \[P_{ {@j@} } = {@exd(lcb[kP])@} + \frac{ {@exd(pp)@} - {@cfb(kP)@} }{ {@f[kP]@} } \times 10 \approx {@Pd@}\]</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
